    spi: fix IDR collision on systems with both fixed and dynamic SPI bus n=
umbers
    =

    On systems where some controllers get a dynamic ID assigned and some ha=
ve
    a fixed number from DT, the current implemention might run into an IDR
    collision if the dynamic controllers gets probed first and get an IDR n=
umber,
    which is later requested by the controller with the fixed numbering. Wh=
en
    this happens the fixed controller will fail to register with the SPI co=
re.
    =

    Fix this by skipping all known alias numbers when assigning the dynamic=
 IDs.
    =

    Fixes: 9b61e302210e (spi: Pick spi bus number from Linux idr or spi ali=
as)
    Signed-off-by: Lucas Stach <l.stach@pengutronix.de>
    Signed-off-by: Mark Brown <broonie@kernel.org>

